Add Massachusetts behind a state switcher

The app now carries two states. NH and MA data live under data/<state>/ and
load on demand, so switching costs one fetch and nothing is downloaded that
you do not look at.

Massachusetts zones were built the same way as New Hampshire: by routing
along the actual roads named in the MassWildlife boundary description. The
three zones add up to the state outline exactly - 4,754 + 12,650 + 9,933 =
27,337 sq km. One exception, noted in the app: the street-level jog through
Taunton and Somerset on the Coastal boundary is approximated.

Data from MassGIS: 27,034 water bodies at 1:25,000, 2,663 river reaches,
282 Office of Fishing and Boating Access sites, 3,433 open-space parcels
over 50 acres, 351 municipalities. Twelve NOAA tide stations from
Newburyport to Nantucket. Season dates, bag limits and the zone text come
from mass.gov.

Massachusetts closes all hunting on Sundays, so the date control and every
zone read closed on a Sunday.

